/-!
# D4 graph-field tensors: constructions and assembly lemmas

The exported constructions use actual rational irreducible basic factors and
actual tensor actions. Their finrank is the product of the factor finranks,
and the one-factor intertwiner includes the case `n = 1`. The forward-wrapped
weight sequence has period `3*n`, and its period test reduces to the first `n`
labels. The orientation lemmas check both the genuine `StandardModel` action
and the convention of `BinaryDegree.TensorData`.

`character_period_of_classification_and_coefficient_equiv` is conditional:
finite irreducibility, tensor parameter uniqueness, and coefficient-twist
intertwiners must still be supplied. Rational Steinberg tensor irreducibility
and classification on restriction to the subgroup generated by two-elements
are not proved by the present exports. In particular, the definitions of that
subgroup and the full fixed-point group remain distinct.

Source: GLS3, Theorems 2.8.2 and 2.8.5, Corollary 2.8.6(a), Remark 2.8.8;
Aschbacher--Smith, printed p.356 (PDF p.367).
-/
